---
import Base from "@layouts/Base.astro";
import Kickoff from "@components/Kickoff.astro";
import TextImageSection from "@components/TextImageSection.astro";
import Section from "@components/Section.astro"

import kickoffPhoto from "@images/kickoff-feb26.jpg"
---

<Base title="From TechGamesPlus to Tailias" description="A post about my change from TGP to Tailias">
    <Kickoff contentAlign="center" backgroundImage={kickoffPhoto} backgroundAlt="A photo of a whiteboard. It contains a teddy bear drawing on the left and text on the right that says '19 Days until FurDU :3'">
        <h1>From TechGamesPlus to Tailias</h1>
        <p>
            From July 28th, 2026, I am retiring the "TechGamesPlus" branding in favour of "Tailias". This page explains why.
        </p>
    </Kickoff>
    <Section contentAlign="left">
        <p><u>
            Published: <b>July 28th, 2026</b>
        </u></p>
        <p>
            If you've come to visit this website through the "techgamesplus.net" link, you will, of course, find yourself at this page on a new random "tailias.net" website. But who is Tailias? Well, for starters, be rest assured that both TechGamesPlus and Tailias are the same person (me, by the way).
        </p>
    </Section>
    <Section contentAlign="left">
        <h3>
            TL;DR
        </h3>
        <p>
            I'm rebranding myself online to Tailias, effectively retiring the TechGamesPlus branding.
        </p>
    </Section>
    <Section contentAlign="left">
        <h3>
            Retiring the TechGamesPlus Branding
        </h3>
        <p>
            I've had the name "TechGamesPlus" as my online identity name since about early-2020. During this time, I was 12-years-old, had just entered high school, and was forced into isolation because of the COVID-19 pandemic. Prior to this, I remember having referred to myself as the most cringiest 2010s-YouTube-esque names ever: "MyCraftU2" and "Da Beef".<br/>
            <br/>
            "MyCraftU2" stuck for a little bit, and was actually a decent name for the time, yet I remember the confusion of my friends when talking about the name, referring to it sometimes as "Minecraft YouTube", which was fair.<br/>
            <br/>
            "Da Beef", on the other hand, lived longer than I should've let it.<br/>
            <br/>
            Yet historically, the name "TechGamesPlus" came along one day as I was riding around the backyard, mumbling to myself as I tried not to crash the Powerwing. I had imaginary friends back then (still do sometimes but not these ones) and I was mumbling on about how one of my friends made a game and had the copyright claimed against them by a company named, you guessed it, "TechGamesPlus" - Well, at the time, it was more "TechGames+" as the symbol instead of the word "Plus", I'll get to that. Ever since, that name just stuck with me.<br/>
            <br/>
            At some point after I had gotten back to school, I started making YouTube videos. I had done this before as "MyCraftU2", yet ended up shutting that down. I tried again as "Da Beef", yet was caught doing so, thus forced to close it at the hands of my mother. I tried briefly again as "TechGames+", but apparently YouTube wouldn't accept the "+", hence why it changed to the word.<br/>
            <br/>
            Fast forward a few months and I had formed the UnderscoreSquad whilst we were still in our pre-CODEC era, and the nickname of "TGP" starting coming more into fruition than anything else. Since then, I haven't really bothered changing it as it became a more staple name to my identity.<br/>
            <br/>
            Yet, over time, I've started to feel like the "TechGamesPlus" branding is just wearing off. In short, I can always call myself "TGP", yet people just wonder why I do that? Heck, it was even the name I put down on my FurDU 2026 con badge. I've been wanting to stick to, at some point, making it a "T&G" branding, with videos coming out under "T&G Productions", but that never came to fruition.
        </p>
    </Section>
    <Section contentAlign="left">
        <h3>
            So why "Tailias"?
        </h3>
        <p>
            Long story short: <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Furry_fandom" target="_blank">I'm a furry</a>. If you don't like that fact, then fuck off.<br/>
            <br/>
            For nearly five years, I've been claiming that I'm a furry. At that time, I was starting to delve into the furry fandom a little bit (with thanks to channels like <a href="https://www.twitch.tv/betaetadelota" target="_blank">BetaEtaDelota</a> and visual novel games such as <a href="https://cockhole.itch.io/9-22" target="_blank">9:22</a>.<br/>
            <br/>
            Hilariously, I "became" a furry out of spite of one of my ex-friends, who used to brag a bunch about wanting to kill furries. He was bragging one day about this TikTok account he made where all the videos were simply just that shitty TikTok voice saying "Finding furry hunters 5 out of 100k" and clips of him wearing a paper mache mask and revealing a fake gun inside a case. Yet, since that date, I don't regret my decisions.<br/>
            <br/>
            Of course, that day I remember growling and hissing, scratching the wall in rage. "How dare he wish death upon a community like that?!" I had no clue what furries actually were until now. I'm 18 (nearly 19) (at the time of publication) and am much more mature. I know more about this fandom than I could've ever known five years ago.<br/>
            <br/>
            Tailias came into fruition the moment <a href="https://www.astrisfursuits.com/" target="_blank">Astris</a> concluded her Guest of Honour panel at FurDU 2026. Her panel was all about how to make a fursuit, which mostly consisted of sewing materials and shit, but she did make a live demonstation of cutting apart a pair of Kmart clothes to show how to stitch clothing. Since that panel, the idea of having a fursona for myself was starting to rapidly grow. I started wanting to make a suit, but had no reference to base it off of. Yet, I've always wanted to adapt Terror Teddy into a fursona of some kind.<br/>
            <br/>
            Eventually, a month after walking out of FurDU with no sona whatsoever, I finally have "Tailias" with massive thanks to <a href="https://twitter.com/Sockune" target="_blank">Michaela (@Sockune) on Twitter</a>, and even further commissioned my main photo from <a href="https://www.sioteru.com/" target="_blank">Sioteru</a>.<br/>
            <br/>
            So, in terms of my rebrand, I'm becoming more "furry centric" or whatever the term is. I want to become more involved into this fandom. I felt like the TechGamesPlus branding was dying on me, so that's why I'm switching from TGP to Tailias.
        </p>
    </Section>
    <Section contentAlign="left">
        <h3>
            What'll happen to the TechGamesPlus brand?
        </h3>
        <p>
            In terms of the domain <u>techgamesplus.net</u>, this will not expire until April 2027. Until then, that domain will reroute to this page on <u>tailias.net</u>.<br/>
            <br/>
            Terror Teddy will be a personal asset to my life, and as such will represent that half. He's too unique of a character to even partially let go.<br/>
            <br/>
            Tee Tee, my cartoon adaptation, will remain a mix of both.
        </p>
    </Section>
</Base>
<style>
    h3 {
        text-decoration: underline;
    }
</style>